    {
      "id": "fashion-tshirt-short-sleeves",
      "topicId": "fashion",
      "sourceOrder": 1,
      "status": "READY_FOR_SAME_READER_FINAL",
      "literalGroups": [
        {
          "group": "prompt_ordered_answers_key",
          "literal": {
            "prompt": "Как называется хлопковая нижняя одежда без воротника с короткими рукавами?",
            "answers": [
              "Футболка",
              "Рубашка-поло",
              "Свитер",
              "Блузка"
            ],
            "correctIndex": 0
          },
          "literalSHA256": "3f88ac9a6ddc878cbcaeebd1d16c7a434879251c909078ade4279aeff5917d78",
          "primaryGround": "Merriam-Webster defines T-shirt as a collarless short-sleeved or sleeveless, usually cotton undershirt (T-shirt L40-L42/L97-L103). The options are upper-body garments; polo has a collar (polo L36), a usual shirt has a collar/front opening (shirt L40-L44), a sweater is knitted/crocheted (sweater L46), and a blouse is often loose (blouse L58).",
          "sourcePaths": [
            "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17abf/source-fashion1/raw-tshirt.json",
            "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17abf/source-fashion1/raw-polo-shirt.json",
            "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17abf/source-fashion1/raw-shirt.json",
            "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17abf/source-fashion1/raw-sweater.json",
            "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17abf/source-fashion1/raw-blouse.json"
          ],
          "locator": "Exact Merriam-Webster lines noted in primaryGround; full native source capture is listed in rawSources.",
          "sourcePathsBeforeTechnicalNormalization": [
            "/Users/eaafonasev/.codex/worktrees/question-quality-wave6-01a12b0f/mindbattle/docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17abf/source-fashion1/raw-tshirt.json",
            "/Users/eaafonasev/.codex/worktrees/question-quality-wave6-01a12b0f/mindbattle/docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17abf/source-fashion1/raw-polo-shirt.json",
            "/Users/eaafonasev/.codex/worktrees/question-quality-wave6-01a12b0f/mindbattle/docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17abf/source-fashion1/raw-shirt.json",
            "/Users/eaafonasev/.codex/worktrees/question-quality-wave6-01a12b0f/mindbattle/docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17abf/source-fashion1/raw-sweater.json",
            "/Users/eaafonasev/.codex/worktrees/question-quality-wave6-01a12b0f/mindbattle/docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17abf/source-fashion1/raw-blouse.json"
          ]
        },
        {
          "group": "explanation",
          "literal": "Футболка — обычно хлопковая нижняя одежда без воротника с короткими рукавами. Рубашка-поло обычно прилегающая и имеет воротник; свитер вяжут или вяжут крючком, а блузка обычно свободно закрывает тело от шеи до талии.",
          "literalSHA256": "bafdf49a756881334a32d0e66f6fd2f444a80323281436ff8ea94189c2811987",
          "primaryGround": "T-shirt definition: Merriam-Webster L40-L42; polo collar/fit L36; sweater L46; blouse L58.",
          "sourcePaths": [
            "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17abf/source-fashion1/raw-tshirt.json",
            "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17abf/source-fashion1/raw-polo-shirt.json",
            "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17abf/source-fashion1/raw-sweater.json",
            "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17abf/source-fashion1/raw-blouse.json"
          ],
          "locator": "Exact Merriam-Webster lines noted in primaryGround; full native source capture is listed in rawSources.",
          "sourcePathsBeforeTechnicalNormalization": [
            "/Users/eaafonasev/.codex/worktrees/question-quality-wave6-01a12b0f/mindbattle/docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17abf/source-fashion1/raw-tshirt.json",
            "/Users/eaafonasev/.codex/worktrees/question-quality-wave6-01a12b0f/mindbattle/docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17abf/source-fashion1/raw-polo-shirt.json",
            "/Users/eaafonasev/.codex/worktrees/question-quality-wave6-01a12b0f/mindbattle/docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17abf/source-fashion1/raw-sweater.json",
            "/Users/eaafonasev/.codex/worktrees/question-quality-wave6-01a12b0f/mindbattle/docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17abf/source-fashion1/raw-blouse.json"
          ]
        },
        {
          "group": "note0",
          "literal": "Футболку также используют как верхнюю рубашку сходного дизайна.",
          "literalSHA256": "5c49da9ef0a83f1ecc6211057c9e53fa1547d863ad9099517461ef97bad994f4",
          "primaryGround": "Merriam-Webster says T-shirt can also mean an outer shirt of similar design (L42), beyond the prompt/key.",
          "sourcePaths": [
            "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17abf/source-fashion1/raw-tshirt.json"
          ],
          "locator": "Exact Merriam-Webster lines noted in primaryGround; full native source capture is listed in rawSources.",
          "sourcePathsBeforeTechnicalNormalization": [
            "/Users/eaafonasev/.codex/worktrees/question-quality-wave6-01a12b0f/mindbattle/docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17abf/source-fashion1/raw-tshirt.json"
          ]
        },
        {
          "group": "note1",
          "literal": "Рубашка-поло обычно прилегающая, часто трикотажная и с воротником; рукава бывают короткими или длинными.",
          "literalSHA256": "f4be7f61b691f39d70c15869e3b25cbeaaf241a280fae607def1a04c55624d05",
          "primaryGround": "Merriam-Webster defines a polo shirt as a close-fitting pullover, often knit, with short or long sleeves and a turnover collar or banded neck (L36).",
          "sourcePaths": [
            "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17abf/source-fashion1/raw-polo-shirt.json"
          ],
          "locator": "Exact Merriam-Webster lines noted in primaryGround; full native source capture is listed in rawSources.",
          "sourcePathsBeforeTechnicalNormalization": [
            "/Users/eaafonasev/.codex/worktrees/question-quality-wave6-01a12b0f/mindbattle/docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17abf/source-fashion1/raw-polo-shirt.json"
          ]
        },
        {
          "group": "note2",
          "literal": "Свитер может быть вязаным или связанным крючком.",
          "literalSHA256": "8b3dd28faadabcc251370b7d61ce73a30e8527c40e2adc904e35e403f5ad5e41",
          "primaryGround": "The retained Merriam-Webster clothing sense 2a says sweater is knitted or crocheted (L42-L46). The repair states only this shared construction fact about Russian «свитер»; it does not translate the broader English senses “jacket” or “pullover” into Russian garment categories.",
          "sourcePaths": [
            "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17abf/source-fashion1/raw-sweater.json"
          ],
          "locator": "Merriam-Webster complete clothing sense 2a L42-L46; full body reused from initial raw capture.",
          "sourcePathsBeforeTechnicalNormalization": [
            "/Users/eaafonasev/.codex/worktrees/question-quality-wave6-01a12b0f/mindbattle/docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17abf/source-fashion1/raw-sweater.json"
          ]
        },
        {
          "group": "note3",
          "literal": "Блузка часто бывает свободной и закрывает тело от шеи до талии.",
          "literalSHA256": "116031714b436e2bf7103807fb43aa2640ffa834654b9852f7fc075d0f0f952e",
          "primaryGround": "Merriam-Webster defines a blouse as a usually loose-fitting garment covering the body from neck to waist (L58).",
          "sourcePaths": [
            "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17abf/source-fashion1/raw-blouse.json"
          ],
          "locator": "Exact Merriam-Webster lines noted in primaryGround; full native source capture is listed in rawSources.",
